WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.095
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Thursday, October twenty second.

2
00:00:05.095 --> 00:00:15.780
Five minutes on the last twenty four hours of security developments, from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

3
00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.580
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:23.575
We start with a travel advisory change we hadn't yet covered.

5
00:00:23.575 --> 00:00:31.320
On Monday, October nineteenth, the State Department raised Kenya from Level 2, Exercise Increased Caution, to Level 3, Reconsider Travel.

6
00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:41.881
The advisory cites health, crime, kidnapping, terrorism, unrest and traffic safety, and it notes the CDC travel health notice for Ebola in Kenya.

7
00:00:41.881 --> 00:00:57.721
It says Do Not Travel to the Eastleigh and Kibera neighborhoods of Nairobi, to Garissa, Wajir, Mandera, Lamu and Tana River counties, northern Kilifi and the coast north of Malindi, to West Pokot and western Turkana, and to areas within fifty kilometers of the Ethiopian border in Marsabit and Turkana.

8
00:00:57.721 --> 00:01:03.030
It warns that al Shabaab is active in the border and coastal areas.

9
00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:07.220
This change could have repercussions for ministries and volunteer teams working in Kenya.

10
00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:10.065
Next, Saudi Arabia.

11
00:01:10.065 --> 00:01:28.736
The State Department spokesperson says the department issued an ordered departure for non-emergency US government employees and their family members in Saudi Arabia only, citing Houthi attacks on Saudi civilian airports and other critical infrastructure that caused civilian casualties and severe travel disruptions.

12
00:01:28.736 --> 00:01:32.538
He called an earlier Reuters report of a Gulf-wide departure inaccurate.

13
00:01:32.538 --> 00:01:41.358
Reuters also reports Saudi civil aviation saying one person was killed and eight injured in an attack on King Fahd airport in Dammam.

14
00:01:41.358 --> 00:01:49.971
And the TRAC terrorism account reports a Houthi attack on Saudi military cargo planes at Al Rayyan airport in Hadhramaut, Yemen.

15
00:01:49.971 --> 00:02:06.064
On cyber, Reuters reports a critical vulnerability in PHP, the programming language behind a large share of the world's websites, led governments across Europe to take sites offline until a patch is installed, and Asian governments are stepping up their defenses.

16
00:02:06.064 --> 00:02:12.939
The Institute for the Study of War took its own website offline as a precaution after warnings from US cyber authorities.

17
00:02:12.939 --> 00:02:27.634
Separately, Microsoft says a China state aligned group it calls Storm zero nine forty used an AI penetration testing tool to automate attacks on hundreds of organizations worldwide, and was behind the recent ConnectWise supply chain compromise.

18
00:02:27.634 --> 00:02:38.931
On sanctions, the Treasury Department sanctioned a Panama and Greece based law firm, along with shipping agents and vessels, for supporting illicit Iranian shipping.

19
00:02:38.931 --> 00:02:41.342
A few updates on stories we've covered.

20
00:02:41.342 --> 00:02:50.377
Update on the Ebola outbreak: Australia's Smartraveller says Nigeria has introduced strict entry requirements after its confirmed case in Abuja.

21
00:02:50.377 --> 00:02:59.793
Update on Typhoon Champi: Reuters reports Taiwan issued a land warning and cancelled more than a hundred flights as the storm passes its northeastern coast.

22
00:02:59.793 --> 00:03:09.465
Update on northern Ethiopia: the UK Foreign Office has updated its travel advice with new information on the conflict, including the Tigray region.

23
00:03:09.465 --> 00:03:13.589
Now a few quick notes by region.

24
00:03:13.589 --> 00:03:27.871
In the Middle East, Reuters reports US congressional candidate Brad Lander was detained by Israeli forces in the West Bank, along with other Americans and Israelis who were harvesting olives with Palestinian farmers, according to rights groups.

25
00:03:27.871 --> 00:03:36.442
The UN humanitarian office, OCHA, says nearly two hundred sixty thousand people in Yemen have been displaced by fighting since August, half of them seeking refuge in Taiz.

26
00:03:36.442 --> 00:03:47.447
The Institute for the Study of War says Iran may have used more accurate weapons against commercial shipping in the Strait of Hormuz over the past two weeks.

27
00:03:47.447 --> 00:04:01.707
In Africa, TRAC reports al Shabaab assaults on militia bases near Kismayo and on a Ugandan military base in Lower Shabelle, Somalia, and an Islamic State attack on Congolese army forces in Ituri province, Congo.

28
00:04:01.707 --> 00:04:21.526
In South Asia, TRAC reports suspected Pakistani Taliban militants abducted sugar mill employees from a bus in Dera Ismail Khan district, an Islamic State Khorasan killing of a Pakistani intelligence officer in Bajaur, and attacks on Taliban police and checkpoints in Afghanistan's Ghazni and Parwan provinces.

29
00:04:21.526 --> 00:04:33.413
In Latin America, TRAC reports an army soldier died after an ELN linked roadside bomb in Arauca, Colombia, and security forces captured an ELN drone operator in Cesar department.

30
00:04:33.413 --> 00:04:37.579
In Europe, Reuters reports Germany's military is warning of a significant Russian sabotage threat.

31
00:04:37.579 --> 00:04:46.738
ACLED says protests in France have surged to around sixty five a day, more than three times the usual average, with nearly one in four involving riots.

32
00:04:46.738 --> 00:04:49.403
That's today's brief.

33
00:04:49.403 --> 00:04:59.200
It summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

34
00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:01.383
This brief is digitally narrated.

35
00:05:01.383 --> 00:05:02.434
Questions?

36
00:05:02.434 --> 00:05:05.960
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

37
00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:08.116
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
